{"name":"Pansy Posie","hex":"#bfa7b6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pansy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cultivated flowering plant, derived by hybridization within species Viola tricolor.","A deep purple colour, like that of the pansy."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Wimpy; spineless; feeble.","Of a deep purple colour, like that of the pansy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pansy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pansy","blocks":[{"text":"The garden pansy is a type of polychromatic large-flowered hybrid plant cultivated as a garden flower. It is derived by hybridization from several species in the section Melanium of the genus Viola, particularly V. tricolor, a wildflower of Europe and western Asia known as heartsease. It is sometimes known as V. tricolor var. hortensis, but this scientific name is suspect. While V. tricolor var. hortensis Groenland & Rümpler is a synonym of Viola × wittrockiana, V. tricolor var. hortensis DC. refers to a horticultural variety of wild pansy that had been illustrated in Flora Danica in 1777 before the existence of Viola × wittrockiana."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/PansyScan_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-PansyScan_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pansy","wikidata":"Q12861234"},{"title":"Nosegay","blocks":[{"text":"A nosegay, posy, or tussie-mussie is a small flower bouquet. They have existed in some form since at least medieval times, when they were carried or worn around the head or bodice. Doilies are traditionally used to bind the stems in these arrangements. Alternatively, \"posy holders\", available in a variety of shapes and materials, enable the wearing of these arrangements \"at the waist, in the hair, or secured with a brooch\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/The_nosegay_LCCN2002710681.jpg/330px-The_nosegay_LCCN2002710681.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nosegay","wikidata":"Q14125324"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Pansy_Flower.jpg/500px-Pansy_Flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Pansy_Flower.jpg/500px-Pansy_Flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pansy flower","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APansy_Flower.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Purple_and_black_viola_cultivar_in_Toronto.jpg/500px-Purple_and_black_viola_cultivar_in_Toronto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Purple_and_black_viola_cultivar_in_Toronto.jpg/500px-Purple_and_black_viola_cultivar_in_Toronto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pansy displaying the two upper overlapping petals, the two side petals, and the single bottom petal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APurple_and_black_viola_cultivar_in_Toronto.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Pansy_bi_colour.jpg/500px-Pansy_bi_colour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Pansy_bi_colour.jpg/1280px-Pansy_bi_colour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Pansy_bi_colour.jpg/500px-Pansy_bi_colour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A bicolor pansy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APansy_bi_colour.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/C